      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Retained foreign bodies are not infrequent following surgical procedures and are associated with medico-legal issues. Gossypiboma following ocular surgeries is rare but should be included in the differential diagnosis of a postoperative patient presenting with pain or mass. We report on one such case of gossypiboma following surgical excision of lacrimal gland."},
